---
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro';
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '@/site';

const skills = [
  {
    group: 'Where the evidence is deepest',
    items: [
      'Python + asyncio',
      'LLM pipeline engineering: prompt architecture, structured output, JSON repair, batching, fallback chains, token and cost tracking',
      'RAG design: retrieval, evidence ranking, citation grounding',
      'gRPC / Protocol Buffers, including proto evolution',
      'PostgreSQL',
      'Docker',
      'Evaluation and ablation methodology',
      'Production computer vision: pose, tracking, re-identification, detection, calibration',
    ],
  },
  {
    group: 'Strong, used in production',
    items: [
      'TypeScript / Node (NestJS, Fastify), React Native',
      'Supabase / row-level security',
      'Redis, including Lua scripting',
      'MinIO / S3, Qdrant',
      'CI/CD: GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, semantic-release',
      'Security assessment: authorisation auditing, pentest methodology, auth hardening',
      'Streaming APIs: gRPC streaming, SSE, WebSocket',
    ],
  },
  {
    group: 'Supporting',
    items: ['PyTorch, TensorFlow, scikit-learn', 'Next.js, Prisma', 'nginx, Azure, Expo/EAS'],
  },
];
---

<Base title="About" description="Who I am, how I work, and what I am strongest at.">
  <PageHeader title="About" />
  <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[3fr_2fr]">
    <div class="prose-site">
      <p>
        I'm a machine learning engineer in Munich. Since 2023 I've worked at Semorai, a German
        software company with automotive and manufacturing enterprise clients, on an LLM
        document-intelligence platform. I built the first version of its requirement-extraction
        service and was the primary developer of the rewrite — about half of all commits, most of
        the integration and release work, 219 automated releases. I co-developed the shared LLM
        gateway every service on the platform calls through.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside work I'm co-founder and CTO of Olber, a services marketplace in Uzbekistan with a
        real-money escrow wallet, live on both app stores with over ten thousand registered users.
        Three of us built and operate it in evenings and weekends.
      </p>
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>
        I start from production output, not from the design doc. Most of what I'm proud of began as
        a root-cause analysis of something wrong in a real result — a standards code spelled four
        ways, a citation nobody could open, a stream that died at exactly sixty seconds. The fix
        usually made the model do less: deterministic code first, the model last, and only asked the
        one question it's good at.
      </p>
      <p>
        I write a lot of tests — 21,000 lines into one suite — because the systems I build run for
        minutes and fail in ways a unit test can't see. I'd rather ship a hedged number than an
        impressive one. And I like being the person who integrates other people's work and cuts the
        release.
      </p>
      <h2>Before Munich</h2>
      <p>
        School in Tashkent, a computer science degree at Riga Technical University (thesis on
        skin-lesion classification, 96.94% on HAM10000 with a caveat I'm happy to discuss), a first
        job two months into the first semester, five hackathon placements across Riga, Helsinki and
        St. Gallen, and a student community in Riga I helped run. The
        <a href="/journey">journey page</a> has the map.
      </p>
      <p>
        English and Russian fluently, Uzbek natively, German as a beginner. Authorised to work in
        Germany.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside>
      <h2 class="text-ink mb-4 text-base font-semibold">Skills, by strength of evidence</h2>
      {
        skills.map((s) => (
          <section class="mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-faint mb-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-wide uppercase">{s.group}</h3>
            <ul class="m-0 list-none space-y-1 p-0">
              {s.items.map((item) => (
                <li class="text-ink border-line border-l-2 pl-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">{item}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </section>
        ))
      }
      <p class="text-muted mt-6 text-sm">
        CV: <a class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4" href={site.cvPath}>PDF</a>
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Base>
